The low-resolution sweep of the blowup ("vortex") problem across all four
rungs and a ladder in K, run to t_star (doc/dfmm_3d.md Sec. 7 Stage 5,
doc/incompressible.md Sec. 0).

Compile ONE binary for all four rungs; ALWAYS make clean when changing INIT=
or DFMM=.
    cd bin && make clean && make COMPILER=METAL NDIM=3 HYDRO=1 DFMM=4 INIT=BLOWUP

  rung 1  incompressible=.true.   incomp_stress='viscous'   (Newtonian, div u = 0)
  rung 2  incompressible=.false.  dfmm_closure='ns'         (Newtonian, compressible)
  rung 3  incompressible=.false.  dfmm_closure='evolve'     (moments,  compressible)
  rung 4  incompressible=.true.   incomp_stress='moment'    (moments,  div u = 0)

Each pair differs in ONE namelist entry, so the 2x2 isolates closure from
compressibility.  Do not write an ampersand-prefixed group name in this
header: gfortran's namelist reader treats it as the start of that group.

WHAT t_star IS, AND WHY IT IS blowup_delta.
The note parameterises the construction by the REMAINING time
Delta = t_star - t (its Eq. 17), and the strain at the origin is exactly
S(0,t) = (1/Delta) diag(-2,-2,4), ||S||_op = 4/Delta (its Eq. 19).  The
initial condition here freezes that field at Delta = blowup_delta, so in the
construction's own clock the remaining time at t = 0 IS blowup_delta and

    t_star = blowup_delta ,        t_def = blowup_delta/4 .

Running to t = t_star is therefore running four deformation times, i.e. all
the way to the construction's singular time.  The earlier namelists
(dfmm_blowup3d.nml, incomp_blowup3d.nml) stop at tout = Delta/4 = t_star/4,
one deformation time; this sweep goes to t_star and samples the quarters, so
the ORDERING of the indicator failures in time is visible rather than a
single snapshot.

IMPORTANT CAVEAT.  There is no forcing.  The construction needs a smooth
external force to stay on its trajectory; condinit sets the instantaneous
local strain field and lets the gas evolve freely from it (see
hydro/condinit.f90, #if INIT==BLOWUP).  So this is NOT a simulation of the
construction, and the flow does not actually blow up at t_star.  The
question it answers is the note's question: starting from the constructed
state at remaining time Delta, do the assumptions that make a velocity-only
description possible survive?  t_star is the reference clock, not a
predicted event in the run.

CALIBRATION (Family B, holding the dissipation time equal to the deformation
time; derivation in namelist/dfmm_blowup3d.nml).  With
    Delta = 0.4483/sqrt(K) ,     dfmm_tau = 0.056037*sqrt(K)
the governing group K = 8 mu/(p Delta) = 8 dfmm_tau/Delta is reproduced to
1e-5, and the Newtonian prediction is lam_min(P_NS)/p = 1 - K, so rung 2
should cross zero at K = 1 while rungs 3 and 4 should not.

    K      Delta = t_star   dfmm_tau     Ma      lam_min(P_NS)/p
   ------------------------------------------------------------
   0.10       1.41765       0.01772     0.348        +0.90
   0.25       0.89660       0.02802     0.550        +0.75
   0.50       0.63399       0.03962     0.778        +0.50
   1.00       0.44830       0.05604     1.100         0.00
   2.00       0.31700       0.07925     1.556        -1.00
   3.00       0.25883       0.09706     1.905        -2.00

The Ma column is why the compressible rungs cannot be run at large K and
small Mach at once: a one-mode field forces Kn*Ma = 0.494 K.  That confound
is the reason rungs 1 and 4 exist.

OUTPUT TIMES.  tout below is the K = 1 quarter ladder,
t_star*(1/4, 1/2, 3/4, 1); scale all four by sqrt(1/K) for another rung of
the ladder.  tout_exact=.true. is REQUIRED here, not optional: the
deliverable is the value of an indicator AT a stated fraction of t_star, and
without it the snapshot lands up to a full dt past the request (measured:
0.9% on Metal, 11.9% on the CUDA sedov test).

KNOWN LIMITATION.  Rung 4 DIVERGES at K >= 1 at this resolution: |Pi|/p_0
grows without bound in a resolved mode and incomp_step stops the run when it
passes 100 rather than let a sweep script tabulate the resulting -inf as a
realizability violation.  The cause is not established -- see
doc/incompressible.md Section 4c for the three things it has been ruled out
as (aliasing, a CFL limit, and anything specific to Q) and for the decisive
next diagnostic.  Rung 4 results here are trustworthy for K <= 0.5 only.
Rungs 1, 2 and 3 are unaffected and complete at every K in the table.

Rung 1 reports min lam(P)/p0 = 1.000 identically, because it carries no Pi.
Read that as "not applicable", not as a passing check: it is the
pressure-gauge argument of doc/incompressible.md Section 0 appearing in the
output.  Check 7 cannot be asked of rung 1, which is why rung 4 exists.

CLOSURE ORDER.  Build this namelist with EITHER
    DFMM=1  ->  NVAR=10, ten-moment    (rho, rho u, P_ij)
    DFMM=4  ->  NVAR=38, twenty-moment + dual frame
Use DFMM=1 for any published number.  The twenty-moment system is NOT
hyperbolic on the states this problem visits -- it loses hyperbolicity inside
the realizability cone, in a Q-dependent region -- so its runs diverge under
refinement (level 5 at K=3, level 6 at K=2 and 3) and cannot answer check 7.
The ten-moment system is hyperbolic wherever P > 0 (Levermore), converges, and
reaches max|Pi|/p = 1.62 without trouble.  See doc/incompressible.md Sec. 4d
and 4e.

RUNG 4 CARRIES AN EXTRA PARAMETER.  incomp_p0 sets the Mach number, and the
rung-4 answer to check 7 depends on it: at K=2 level 4, incomp_p0 = 0.25 and
1.0 cross the cone while 4.0 survives to t_star, at essentially identical
max|u|.  Pi scales with p0 and so does the -div Pi force in the momentum
equation, so |Pi|/p0 is not invariant under rescaling p0.  Always report
incomp_p0, and Mach-match it to the compressible rung being compared: at K=2
the compressible rung reaches Ma = 1.497 and incomp_p0 = 1 reaches 1.502.

RESOLUTION.  levelmin = levelmax = 4 (16^3) is the low-resolution sweep --
cheap enough to run 24 configurations, and adequate for the ORDERING of the
indicators.  It is NOT adequate for their converged values: doc/dfmm_3d.md
Sec. 7 shows sigma_max(dL/dx) and min g are resolution-limited extrema that
keep growing with refinement, so treat Kn_local from this sweep as a lower
bound.  min lam(P)/p does converge and is the number to trust here.

&RUN_PARAMS
hydro=.true.
ncontrol=1000
nrestart=0
nremap=0
nsubcycle=10*1
verbose=.false.
nstepmax=200000
nsuperoct=2
/

&AMR_PARAMS
levelmin=4
levelmax=4
ngridtot=800
ncachemax=800
nexpand=1
boxlen=1.0
/

&INIT_PARAMS
nregion=1
region_type(1)='square'
x_center=0.5
y_center=0.5
z_center=0.5
length_x=10.0
length_y=10.0
length_z=10.0
exp_region=10.0
d_region=1.0
u_region=0.0
v_region=0.0
w_region=0.0
p_region=1.0
/

&BLOWUP_PARAMS
blowup_delta=0.4483
blowup_rho0=1.0
blowup_p0=1.0
blowup_nwave=1
blowup_init_ns=.false.
/

&OUTPUT_PARAMS
foutput=1000000   ! >0 so the tout-driven snapshot fires (amr_step.f90:107)
tout=0.112075,0.22415,0.336225,0.4483
tout_exact=.true. ! REQUIRED: the answer is an indicator AT a fraction of t_star
/

&HYDRO_PARAMS
gamma=1.6666666666666667
courant_factor=0.4
slope_type=1
riemann='hll'
/

&DFMM_PARAMS
! dfmm_tau appears in BOTH groups below and read_params reads INCOMP_PARAMS
! second (amr/read_params.f90:1063), so the INCOMP_PARAMS value wins.  Keep
! them equal; the sweep driver sets both.
dfmm_tau=0.056037
dfmm_prandtl=0.6666666666666667
dfmm_source=.true.
dfmm_closure='evolve'
dfmm_diag=.true.
dfmm_fatal_realizability=.false.
dfmm_ic_sigmax=0.02
/

&INCOMP_PARAMS
incompressible=.false.
incomp_p0=1.0
incomp_rho0=1.0
incomp_stress='moment'
incomp_diag=.true.
dfmm_tau=0.056037
/
